mark german just came out with a new  bombshell report talking about apple's  september event that is happening in  less than one month and he revealed the  apple event date which is totally  unexpected to me because apple usually  hosts their september events on a  tuesday usually the second tuesday of  the month but no he gave us a date of  september 7th which is a wednesday and  he also gave us his reasoning for it  exactly what to expect at this event and  what not to expect because he talked  about some other leaks for other apple  devices coming later this year which i'm  also going to talk about so before i get  into all of those interesting details i  do want to quickly mention the different  devices that we should be expecting at  this september event happening on the  7th first of all we're getting the  iphone 14 lineup which is no longer  going to have a mini model and instead  of that mini we're going to be getting a  larger regular iphone 14 model with a  6.7 inch display for the first time  because you usually have to pay 1100  for the pro max model well not anymore  you're gonna be getting a cheaper iphone  14 plus or max for around 900. but what  i think is going to be really special  this year is actually the pro models  because they are getting some major  changes specifically finally getting rid  of that notch that has been around since  the iphone 10 yes we're moving to a dual  hole punch design with kind of a pill  shape and a hole next to each other and  that is gonna look sweet because it's  gonna allow apple to slam down the  bezels and make them look really nice  and thin and the way they're gonna be  able to do that is by slimming down the  speaker grill to like this razor thin  line at the top of the screen so it's  going to be barely noticeable and it's  going to look amazing now on the other  side we're going to be getting a new 48  megapixel camera that is capable of  shooting 8k video at 60 fps which i  think is going to be amazing this is  going to be the biggest iphone camera  revolution since probably ever this  would be a major difference in terms of  the actual camera quality and apple is  going to be doing it right this year  compared to a lot of the other android  brands that have 8k that looks worse  than apple's 4k and that's because  apple's gonna be building in 8k hevc  h.264 and pro res encoders and decoders  that are going to take the processing  load off of the actual chip itself and  just do that all on the media engine so  it's going to be super efficient and it  shouldn't heat up as much as a lot of  people are expecting so that's going to  be amazing then we also have  three new apple watch models yes all  three are gonna be new because they're  getting rid of the series three so  they're gonna have the apple watch se2  they're gonna have the regular series  eight and a brand new apple watch pro  model which i've made videos talking  about what to expect on that now the  interesting thing is that we just got a  report saying that apple is finally  moving some production of their macbook  and apple watch models over to vietnam  and that's because they want to  diversify their supply chain and have  less reliance on china because there's  some weird things going on there right  now and they're trying to get out of it  slowly so that's a good thing for them  and it means we could have less apple  watch shipping delays which is good for  all of us now mark also mentioned the  10th generation ipad but it seems like  he thinks it's coming later in the fall  which is weird because it usually comes  at apple's september event at least the  last three models that we've had and  specifically in a tweet that he just  posted he confirmed that yes the 10th  generation ipad is coming likely in  october so why the delay well first of  all apple has officially delayed ipad os  16 by about a month which means it's  probably coming in october and on top of  that this is going to be the first major  budget ipad redesigned in many years  with new flat sides apple pencil to  support and a usb type-c port so maybe  that's also why they could be delaying  this model by one month now moving on to  what we should expect interestingly he  didn't mention the airpods pro 2 at all  which is odd because i thought it could  be coming alongside the iphone lineup  because it should be getting upgraded to  bluetooth 5.2 with a new lc3 codec and  lossless support finally but maybe based  on mark's report maybe it's not gonna  come until later in the fall as well so  with that said i am super excited for  this event especially since it's  happening so early in the month so we're  gonna have iphone 14 models in our hands  on september 16th according to mark  german which is less than a month from  today that is amazing now as far as the  reasoning for the event happening on  wednesday the 7th instead of tuesday  mark german tweeted out that the reason  is because monday is labor day leaving  tuesday as a travel day which is why  they chose wednesday the 7th and also  apple did just change their employment  rules requiring employees to return to  the office three times per week starting  september 5th which seems to be a clue  for the event happening on the 7th now  moving on to the other things he  mentioned in his new article mark also  mentioned a couple of new products we  shouldn't expect until later in the fall  and some of these are quite surprising  first of all he believes the m2 ipad pro  models are coming later this year likely  in october which i agree with and those  are expected to come with new wireless  mac safe charging features now we also  mentioned a couple of macs that apple is  apparently looking to launch before the  end of the year including new versions  of the mac mini and high-end macbook  pros with m2 bass processors now this is  interesting because i personally  predicted that those new m2 pro and m2  max macbook pros would not come until  the spring of next year because i  believe apple is going to have a 1.5  year timeline for these macbook releases  especially since we just got the m2  macbook air one and a half years after  the m1 model and i also believe that  apple is going to hold off until the  spring because they want to build their  m2 pro and m2 max chips on tsmc's new  three nanometer process node instead of  the current n5p five nanometer process  node but when i spoke to mark german in  an exclusive interview he disagreed with  that theory and said it should be built  on five nanometer just like the m2  macbook air but honestly it's a really  tough call and he definitely has more  credibility and reputation than i do  but i'm still holding strong with my  thoughts on a spring event launch with  those high-end macbook pros on 3  nanometer instead of 5 nanometer now as  far as the mac mini mark said apple is  planning to launch it this year as well  and i totally agree i think it's  happening in october or november and  we're going to see the mac mini  regardless of whether it's gonna have a  redesign or not which mark thinks it's  not gonna have a redesign i'm still not  really sure about that point maybe apple  will just add some ports to the front of  the current design like the mac studio  who knows but either way we still have  some time to go for those new leaks to  flow in about those mac models but for  now we've got to focus on these awesome  new iphones and apple watches and other  products coming on september 7th so if  you're as excited as i am let me know  down in the comment section below and  click that circle above to subscribe for  more videos like this one thanks for  watching and we'll see you in the next  one  [Music]  you
 

